✅ What is Kubernetes?
Kubernetes (often called K8s) is an open-source container orchestration platform.
 It helps you automate the deployment, scaling, and management of containerized applications — especially when you're running them in a production environment.

💡 Why is Kubernetes useful?
It handles multiple containers (like Docker containers) across a cluster of machines.

If a container fails, Kubernetes can automatically restart it.

It supports load balancing, auto-scaling, and rolling updates.

It ensures high availability and resource optimization.

🛠️ Real-world use case:
Imagine you're running a Java Spring Boot app in Docker. Kubernetes can:

Automatically run multiple instances (pods),

Restart them if they crash,

Distribute incoming traffic using a load balancer,

And scale up/down based on CPU or memory usage.

